}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": counts pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"code":".infinity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When every weight is an integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/numberOfSpanningTrees()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectr